# mkxp-web mruby 2.1.2 patch set #2 (apply AFTER vm.c.patch), from within deps/mruby:
#   patch -p0 --forward < ../../extra/mruby-web.patch
# Found while running Pokemon Essentials v21 (Pokemon Anil) games:
#  1. src/symbol.c  PERF: real hash index for symbol lookup. Stock 2.1.2 has 256 buckets
#     chained by an 8-bit delta and falls back to a LINEAR scan of the whole symbol table
#     once chains get sparse; with tens of thousands of symbols that was ~90% of the CPU
#     time (find_symbol+memcmp) -> ~15x faster frames (38ms -> 2.5ms of Ruby per frame).
#  2. src/vm.c      OP_ARYCAT: copy instead of alias the splatted array. `f(*a, x)` was
#     appending x to the caller's own array `a` (fixed upstream in later mruby).
#  3. src/variable.c  instance variables on Array/String subclasses (e.g. PBAnimation <
#     Array) via a side table, instead of raising "cannot set instance variable".
--- src/symbol.c
+++ src/symbol.c
@@ -123,6 +123,64 @@
